$DIR/test.p:6:30: invalid argument: length -1 (constant of type int) must not be negative
    This error occurs when unsafe.String is called with a length argument that
    is not of integer type, negative, or out of bounds. It also occurs if it is
    used in a package compiled for a language version before go1.20.
    (see "Package unsafe" in the Plutonium spec, section 20.1)
    (run "pluto explain E0146" for a longer explanation)
